WEBVTT

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:11.934
Turn 90 degrees
to the left, please.

00:00:12.045 --> 00:00:14.843
Turn 90 degrees
to the left, please.

00:00:14.914 --> 00:00:18.350
Turn 90 degrees to the right,
please.

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.079
About face.

00:00:25.492 --> 00:00:26.925
Try to hold still, please.

00:00:26.993 --> 00:00:28.756
Is it going to hurt?

00:00:28.828 --> 00:00:29.954
Of course not.

00:00:30.063 --> 00:00:32.861
A few photons
never hurt anybody.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:35.400
We didn't do this last year.

00:00:38.438 --> 00:00:40.633
That's because last
year, I didn't realize

00:00:40.707 --> 00:00:43.505
what an exciting tool
my holo-imager could be

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:45.510
in the pursuit
of medical knowledge.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:48.172
Is something wrong with me?

00:00:48.248 --> 00:00:49.738
Your health is excellent.

00:00:49.816 --> 00:00:50.942
This is just another way

00:00:51.017 --> 00:00:52.848
to make sure
that it stays excellent.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:54.910
Does my mother have to do this?

00:00:54.988 --> 00:00:56.979
Your mother and everybody else
on board.

00:00:57.090 --> 00:00:59.183
I've made it
part of the annual checkup.

00:00:59.259 --> 00:01:00.954
It's quite handy, really.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.756
By attuning
the resonance spectrum

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:03.921
along a subspace band,

00:01:04.064 --> 00:01:05.827
I can take an image
of my patients

00:01:05.899 --> 00:01:08.060
all the way down
to the subatomic level.

00:01:08.134 --> 00:01:09.396
Subatomic level?

00:01:09.469 --> 00:01:11.699
I thought you said
this wasn't going to hurt.

00:01:11.771 --> 00:01:12.897
I did...

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.906
and it won't.

00:01:17.410 --> 00:01:18.934
There... see?

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.842
Nothing to it.

00:01:20.914 --> 00:01:24.645
Try to hold still, please.

00:01:24.717 --> 00:01:26.480
Are you making fun of me?

00:01:26.553 --> 00:01:29.522
No.

00:01:29.589 --> 00:01:31.955
It'll only take a second
to download your images

00:01:32.058 --> 00:01:33.389
into the medical database,

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:35.121
if you'd like to stay
for a moment

00:01:35.195 --> 00:01:37.595
and see what you look like
from the inside out.

00:01:37.664 --> 00:01:39.154
Why not?

00:01:40.366 --> 00:01:42.334
Here we go.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:57.249
Handsome fellow.

00:01:59.586 --> 00:02:01.554
Hmm.

00:02:06.392 --> 00:02:07.859
There's some scar tissue

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:10.122
along the base
of your lower skull.

00:02:10.196 --> 00:02:12.357
Computer, isolate
the occipital plexus,

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:13.490
magnification 500.

00:02:15.702 --> 00:02:17.192
There.

00:02:17.270 --> 00:02:19.830
Scarring along the dura mater.

00:02:19.906 --> 00:02:20.873
From what?

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:22.532
An operation.

00:02:22.609 --> 00:02:25.669
Computer, isolate
the cranial meninges,

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:27.610
magnification 100.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:31.374
More scarring.

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:34.909
No doubt about it,
somebody performed neurosurgery.

00:02:37.123 --> 00:02:38.886
And that somebody...

00:02:38.958 --> 00:02:40.892
was me.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.259
These microlinear incisions
are a dead giveaway.

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:46.730
I developed that procedure
myself.

00:02:46.799 --> 00:02:48.232
I don't understand.

00:02:48.301 --> 00:02:50.701
I don't remember
having an operation.

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:52.738
I'm a little confused as well...

00:02:54.174 --> 00:02:56.233
because I don't remember
performing it.

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:54.827
Who is it?

00:04:54.894 --> 00:04:56.327
The Doctor.

00:04:56.396 --> 00:04:58.261
Come in.

00:04:58.331 --> 00:05:00.731
I've finished giving the crew
their annual physicals.

00:05:00.800 --> 00:05:03.792
But as usual,
the Captain was a no-show.

00:05:03.870 --> 00:05:05.167
Let's get it over with.

00:05:05.238 --> 00:05:06.671
Specific complaints?

00:05:06.739 --> 00:05:08.434
None. How's the crew?

00:05:08.508 --> 00:05:10.499
In good health,
for the most part.

00:05:10.576 --> 00:05:12.669
I found a nascent
alien retrovirus

00:05:12.745 --> 00:05:15.509
bouncing between personnel
on Decks 10 and 11,

00:05:15.581 --> 00:05:17.549
but managed
to nip it in the bud.

00:05:17.617 --> 00:05:19.141
And there's been a little
more wear and tear

00:05:19.218 --> 00:05:20.708
on Seven of Nine's
cranial infrastructure.

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:23.085
I'm going to double
her maintenance routine.

00:05:23.156 --> 00:05:25.556
Cyto-metabolism is normal.

00:05:25.625 --> 00:05:27.525
Endocrine functions functioning.

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.026
That's a relief.

00:05:31.998 --> 00:05:34.398
I'd like you to drop by Sick Bay
at your earliest convenience.

00:05:34.467 --> 00:05:36.799
I've adjusted my holo-imager
for deep body scans.

00:05:36.869 --> 00:05:38.427
You're the only member
of the crew

00:05:38.504 --> 00:05:39.869
who hasn't posed for me yet.

00:05:39.939 --> 00:05:41.304
Maybe next week.

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:42.932
It's a fine instrument, really.

00:05:43.042 --> 00:05:46.671
I've already discovered
something of a mystery with it.

00:05:46.746 --> 00:05:48.236
Apparently, I performed

00:05:48.314 --> 00:05:50.680
a complex neurosurgery
on Harry Kim.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:52.615
According to the isotope decay

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:55.176
around the scars,
it was 18 months ago.

00:05:55.254 --> 00:05:56.380
I don't remember that.

00:05:56.456 --> 00:05:58.356
Neither do I, and...

00:05:58.424 --> 00:05:59.618
neither does the patient.

00:05:59.692 --> 00:06:01.159
I checked my medical entries
for that period.

00:06:01.227 --> 00:06:02.717
There's no mention of surgery.

00:06:02.795 --> 00:06:06.026
Could your holo-imager have
misinterpreted the scans?

00:06:06.099 --> 00:06:07.361
Possibly.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:10.266
The computer is double-checking
the data now.

00:06:10.336 --> 00:06:11.360
I'd also like to run

00:06:11.437 --> 00:06:13.462
a complete diagnostic
on my own program

00:06:13.539 --> 00:06:15.871
and have a look
at my memory files.

00:06:15.942 --> 00:06:17.341
B'Elanna and Harry
are both busy

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:18.741
with the plasma relay repairs.

00:06:18.811 --> 00:06:20.779
Let's make sure you're
next up on the list.

00:06:20.847 --> 00:06:22.246
Thank you, Doctor.

00:06:31.257 --> 00:06:32.519
Hello, Seven.

00:06:32.592 --> 00:06:33.524
Doctor.

00:06:33.593 --> 00:06:34.924
I'm here to ask you a favor.

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.484
Another time.

00:06:36.562 --> 00:06:37.722
I beg your pardon?

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:39.731
I am recalibrating
the deflector dish.

00:06:39.799 --> 00:06:40.731
Come back tomorrow.

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:42.097
I should be finished by then.

00:06:43.169 --> 00:06:45.262
Looks like I'm two for two.

00:06:45.338 --> 00:06:48.569
Oh, the Captain's acting
like she's allergic to me,

00:06:48.641 --> 00:06:49.938
and now my prized pupil

00:06:50.076 --> 00:06:52.306
won't even give me
the time of day.

00:06:55.014 --> 00:06:56.948
State your request.

00:06:57.016 --> 00:06:59.541
A little mystery
has cropped up...

00:06:59.619 --> 00:07:01.951
evidence that I performed
surgery on Ensign Kim

00:07:02.021 --> 00:07:05.388
a year and a half ago,
before you came aboard.

00:07:05.458 --> 00:07:07.892
The trouble is...

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.757
I don't remember it.

00:07:11.030 --> 00:07:13.362
I wanted you to help me run
a self-diagnostic.

00:07:14.634 --> 00:07:16.329
I will assist you...

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:17.869
in one hour.

00:07:17.937 --> 00:07:19.837
Fair enough.

00:07:31.818 --> 00:07:34.309
Computer, locate
the Emergency Medical Hologram.

00:07:34.387 --> 00:07:36.321
The EMH is inactive.

00:07:36.389 --> 00:07:37.651
Activate him.

00:07:37.723 --> 00:07:40.021
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:07:40.092 --> 00:07:42.526
I'm here to assist you,
as I agreed.

00:07:42.595 --> 00:07:45.359
I've run a preliminary
diagnostic of your program.

00:07:45.431 --> 00:07:47.058
Your suspicions were correct.

00:07:47.133 --> 00:07:48.930
I never asked you
to run a diagnostic.

00:07:49.068 --> 00:07:50.933
Suspicions? What
are you talking about?

00:07:51.003 --> 00:07:52.834
You don't recall speaking to me

00:07:52.905 --> 00:07:55.100
in the Astrometrics Lab
one hour ago.

00:07:55.174 --> 00:07:56.766
No.

00:07:56.843 --> 00:07:57.810
The last I remember,

00:07:57.877 --> 00:07:59.811
I was completing
the yearly physicals.

00:07:59.879 --> 00:08:01.369
You mentioned a neurosurgery

00:08:01.447 --> 00:08:03.608
you performed on Ensign Kim
18 months ago.

00:08:03.683 --> 00:08:06.243
Computer, locate the holo-scans

00:08:06.319 --> 00:08:09.186
I took of Ensign Kim
this morning.

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:11.789
Any operation would
show up on...

00:08:11.858 --> 00:08:13.826
Unavailable.
That file has been deleted.

00:08:15.995 --> 00:08:17.656
Let's have a look at my program.

00:08:20.900 --> 00:08:23.835
A deletion in your
short-term memory buffer.

00:08:23.903 --> 00:08:27.066
Our chat in Astrometrics
never got filed.

00:08:27.139 --> 00:08:29.164
That's why I can't remember it.

00:08:29.242 --> 00:08:30.504
Hmm...

00:08:30.576 --> 00:08:32.305
If I were given to paranoia,

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:35.176
I'd say someone is trying
to keep me from finding out

00:08:35.248 --> 00:08:37.409
what happened 18 months ago.

00:08:37.483 --> 00:08:40.145
Hmm...

00:08:40.219 --> 00:08:41.516
My photo album.

00:08:41.587 --> 00:08:42.747
Doctor...

00:08:42.822 --> 00:08:44.619
I was quite a shutterbug
back then.

00:08:44.690 --> 00:08:45.622
Not a day went by

00:08:45.691 --> 00:08:47.921
when I didn't record
an image for posterity.

00:08:48.027 --> 00:08:48.628
Let's have a walk
down memory lane.

00:08:48.628 --> 00:08:50.289
Let's have a walk
down memory lane.

00:08:50.363 --> 00:08:52.024
Meet me on Holodeck 2.

00:09:00.273 --> 00:09:02.639
Computer, display
all holo-images

00:09:02.708 --> 00:09:04.437
taken on Stardate 50979.

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.569
Those holo-images
have been deleted.

00:09:06.646 --> 00:09:07.874
Deleted?

00:09:08.014 --> 00:09:09.481
By whom?

00:09:09.549 --> 00:09:11.517
Unknown.

00:09:13.252 --> 00:09:16.346
I'm detecting residual photons
in the holo-buffer.

00:09:16.422 --> 00:09:19.084
It may be possible
to partially reconstruct

00:09:19.158 --> 00:09:20.420
the images.

00:09:20.493 --> 00:09:21.721
Try.

00:09:24.797 --> 00:09:26.162
I've restored five images.

00:09:26.232 --> 00:09:27.790
They are degraded but intact.

00:09:27.867 --> 00:09:29.835
Let's see them.

00:09:31.804 --> 00:09:33.738
The Mess Hall.

00:09:33.806 --> 00:09:34.830
Do you remember this?

00:09:34.907 --> 00:09:36.465
No.

00:09:36.542 --> 00:09:37.907
Who is that?

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:39.773
The Ensign.

00:09:39.845 --> 00:09:41.312
It seems to be her birthday.

00:09:42.348 --> 00:09:44.282
I've never seen her before.

00:09:47.453 --> 00:09:49.387
The Ensign again.

00:09:49.455 --> 00:09:52.253
I never went on
a shuttle mission with Harry Kim

00:09:52.325 --> 00:09:53.917
and certainly not with her.

00:09:56.662 --> 00:09:58.596
And again.

00:10:18.184 --> 00:10:21.483
I've isolated your memory files
from Stardate 50979.

00:10:21.554 --> 00:10:22.748
They weren't deleted?

00:10:22.822 --> 00:10:23.914
No.

00:10:23.990 --> 00:10:24.922
Then why can't I remember them?

00:10:24.991 --> 00:10:26.083
The program was rewritten

00:10:26.158 --> 00:10:27.921
to deny you access
to those memories.

00:10:28.995 --> 00:10:30.587
I'm trying to restore them.

00:10:33.566 --> 00:10:34.498
Here, here.

00:10:34.567 --> 00:10:35.499
Here, here.

00:10:35.568 --> 00:10:36.500
Say, "Cheese."

00:10:36.569 --> 00:10:38.400
Cheese. Cheese.

00:10:40.339 --> 00:10:41.601
What happened?

00:10:41.674 --> 00:10:43.266
I was in the Mess Hall.

00:10:43.342 --> 00:10:45.435
The files are difficult
to localize.

00:10:45.511 --> 00:10:47.638
The memories will be
out of sequence.

00:10:51.851 --> 00:10:52.783
What was that?

00:10:52.852 --> 00:10:54.183
Our sensors are dead.

00:10:54.253 --> 00:10:56.084
Make a wish.

00:10:57.957 --> 00:10:59.390
They've stopped.

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:01.790
One moment.

00:11:04.630 --> 00:11:05.995
Make a wish.

00:11:15.875 --> 00:11:18.105
I'm going to kill you.

00:11:23.315 --> 00:11:25.180
Ensign, I haven't seen you
in months.

00:11:25.251 --> 00:11:27.549
The price I pay for staying
in good health, I guess.

00:11:27.620 --> 00:11:30.453
Acetylcholine...
25 microliters.

00:11:33.993 --> 00:11:35.153
It's not helping.

00:11:35.227 --> 00:11:37.422
I'm reading
massive synaptic failure.

00:11:37.496 --> 00:11:39.293
That doesn't make any sense.

00:11:46.172 --> 00:11:47.264
This is the last one.

00:11:47.339 --> 00:11:48.271
Say, "Cheese."

00:11:48.340 --> 00:11:49.307
- Cheese.
- Cheese.

00:11:58.784 --> 00:12:00.684
Call the Captain.

00:12:05.791 --> 00:12:09.056
I don't recognize this species.

00:12:09.128 --> 00:12:10.561
Seven?

00:12:10.629 --> 00:12:12.426
They are unknown to the Borg.

00:12:12.498 --> 00:12:14.728
Perhaps these images
have been manipulated.

00:12:14.800 --> 00:12:16.062
No. They're real.

00:12:16.135 --> 00:12:19.104
The image buffer would've
shown signs of tampering.

00:12:19.171 --> 00:12:20.695
I have a different theory.

00:12:20.773 --> 00:12:23.207
I believe there was an attack
on Voyager by this species

00:12:23.275 --> 00:12:26.733
and all our memories
of the event were erased.

00:12:28.314 --> 00:12:30.874
This is the unknown crewman
I told you about...

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:32.713
Ensign Jetal.

00:12:32.785 --> 00:12:35.913
The question is:
Who was she?

00:12:35.988 --> 00:12:39.253
An alien intruder posing
as a Starfleet Ensign?

00:12:39.325 --> 00:12:42.294
Of course, it's impossible
to tell from a photograph,

00:12:42.361 --> 00:12:45.455
but one thing is certain...
we are in immediate danger.

00:12:45.531 --> 00:12:46.657
How so?

00:12:48.334 --> 00:12:49.596
Only a few hours ago,

00:12:49.668 --> 00:12:51.761
as I was beginning
this investigation,

00:12:51.837 --> 00:12:53.805
someone shut down my program

00:12:53.873 --> 00:12:57.172
and eliminated all my memories
of the last 24 hours.

00:12:57.243 --> 00:12:58.972
An intruder may be on board.

00:13:01.413 --> 00:13:02.812
Run a deck-by-deck
security sweep.

00:13:02.882 --> 00:13:04.907
Understood.

00:13:04.984 --> 00:13:07.475
Report to the Astrometrics Lab
and recalibrate the sensors.

00:13:07.553 --> 00:13:11.148
See if you can detect
any cloaked vessels nearby.

00:13:11.223 --> 00:13:13.316
I'll review the medical records
of the rest of the crew.

00:13:13.392 --> 00:13:15.553
Ensign Kim may not
have been the only one

00:13:15.628 --> 00:13:17.459
who was injured
during the attack.

00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:20.021
No. I want you to deactivate
yourself for now.

00:13:20.099 --> 00:13:22.465
We'll erect a security field
around the main computer

00:13:22.535 --> 00:13:24.765
and encrypt all pathways
leading to your program.

00:13:24.837 --> 00:13:26.930
If someone does try
to tamper with you again,

00:13:27.006 --> 00:13:27.938
I want to be ready.

00:13:28.007 --> 00:13:28.939
Captain...

00:13:29.008 --> 00:13:30.168
It's for your own safety,
Doctor.

00:13:30.242 --> 00:13:31.869
Thank you for bringing this
to my attention.

00:13:31.944 --> 00:13:33.571
You will keep me informed?

00:13:33.646 --> 00:13:34.578
Absolutely.

00:13:34.647 --> 00:13:36.080
Dismissed.

00:13:54.333 --> 00:13:56.494
Computer... transfer my program

00:13:56.569 --> 00:13:59.538
from the mobile emitter
to the Sick Bay systems.

00:13:59.605 --> 00:14:01.072
Transfer complete.

00:14:03.943 --> 00:14:05.911
Computer...

00:14:09.448 --> 00:14:11.916
Duplicate all of my memory files

00:14:11.984 --> 00:14:14.544
recorded within
the last 48 hours.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:16.383
Duplication complete.

00:14:16.455 --> 00:14:20.551
Now... I'm going off-line.

00:14:20.626 --> 00:14:23.925
If my program is altered
without my authorization,

00:14:24.029 --> 00:14:27.658
reactivate me and restore
the duplicate memory files.

00:14:27.733 --> 00:14:30.566
Interface with the holo-imaging
device.

00:14:30.636 --> 00:14:32.331
If anybody enters this room,

00:14:32.404 --> 00:14:35.066
commence imaging
in five-second intervals.

00:14:35.140 --> 00:14:37.574
Acknowledged.

00:14:40.813 --> 00:14:43.782
Computer, deactivate EMH.

00:15:28.027 --> 00:15:33.727
Please state the nature
of the medical emergency.

00:15:33.799 --> 00:15:36.233
Hello?

00:15:36.302 --> 00:15:38.236
Restoring memory files.

00:15:41.874 --> 00:15:43.307
Restoration complete.

00:16:16.842 --> 00:16:18.036
Believe me, I was there.

00:16:18.110 --> 00:16:19.099
So was I.

00:16:19.178 --> 00:16:20.907
Commander Chakotay is correct.

00:16:21.013 --> 00:16:22.605
Oh? And how would you know?

00:16:22.681 --> 00:16:24.516
In my youth, I studied
many forms of martial art,

00:16:24.516 --> 00:16:25.312
In my youth, I studied
many forms of martial art,

00:16:25.384 --> 00:16:27.147
including the sumo of Earth.

00:16:27.219 --> 00:16:29.244
I've followed the sport
ever since.

00:16:29.321 --> 00:16:31.084
It was the 77th Emperor's Cup.

00:16:31.156 --> 00:16:33.420
Takashi forced Kar-pek
out of the circle

00:16:33.492 --> 00:16:35.153
in less than three seconds.

00:16:35.227 --> 00:16:36.751
I had a fifth row seat.

00:16:36.829 --> 00:16:39.389
Then you must have been
ordering sake,

00:16:39.465 --> 00:16:41.262
because Takashi's knee
broke the sand

00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:43.392
and the referee gave
the match to Kar-pek.

00:16:43.469 --> 00:16:44.902
Exactly.

00:16:44.970 --> 00:16:47.461
If this is another house call,
it'll have to wait.

00:16:47.539 --> 00:16:49.837
As you can see,
I've got a mutiny on my hands.

00:16:49.908 --> 00:16:53.139
A mutiny? I suppose
that's better than a conspiracy.

00:16:56.548 --> 00:16:57.742
Doctor.

00:16:57.816 --> 00:16:59.374
Tell her, Captain.

00:16:59.451 --> 00:17:03.182
Describe how you tampered
with my program,

00:17:03.255 --> 00:17:05.246
how it was you all along.

00:17:05.324 --> 00:17:08.418
Perhaps you should accompany me
to Sick Bay, Doctor.

00:17:09.862 --> 00:17:12.194
Et tu, Tuvok?

00:17:12.264 --> 00:17:14.391
You're conspiring against me,
all of you.

00:17:14.466 --> 00:17:15.763
Why?

00:17:18.771 --> 00:17:20.636
In my ready room.

00:17:27.479 --> 00:17:29.310
You've been manipulating
my program.

00:17:29.381 --> 00:17:30.348
Don't deny it.

00:17:30.416 --> 00:17:31.781
I don't intend to.

00:17:31.850 --> 00:17:34.375
But... the alien ship...
the intruder...

00:17:34.453 --> 00:17:36.444
Did that attack actually happen?

00:17:36.522 --> 00:17:38.888
Yes. You were damaged
during the incident.

00:17:38.957 --> 00:17:40.788
"Damaged"?

00:17:40.859 --> 00:17:42.918
It caused a conflict
in your programming

00:17:42.995 --> 00:17:44.223
that couldn't be resolved.

00:17:44.296 --> 00:17:45.558
What kind of conflict?

00:17:45.631 --> 00:17:47.496
I had no choice
but to deny you access

00:17:47.566 --> 00:17:49.227
to your memories
of those events.

00:17:49.301 --> 00:17:51.428
What kind of conflict?!

00:17:51.503 --> 00:17:52.435
If I told you that, I might

00:17:52.504 --> 00:17:53.835
set the whole thing
in motion again.

00:17:53.906 --> 00:17:55.669
This "conflict"
in my programming...

00:17:55.741 --> 00:17:57.072
Yes?
That's not good enough.

00:17:57.142 --> 00:17:58.074
It'll have to be.

00:17:58.143 --> 00:17:59.132
Captain!

00:17:59.211 --> 00:18:01.236
I've made a command decision
for your own benefit

00:18:01.313 --> 00:18:02.871
and the welfare
of this entire crew.

00:18:02.948 --> 00:18:04.108
I'm not willing to debate it.

00:18:04.183 --> 00:18:06.117
How would you like it
if I operated on you

00:18:06.185 --> 00:18:08.415
without your consent
or without your knowledge?

00:18:08.487 --> 00:18:09.977
If the operation saved my life?

00:18:10.055 --> 00:18:11.044
I could live with it.

00:18:11.123 --> 00:18:12.021
I don't believe you.

00:18:12.091 --> 00:18:13.991
You'd feel as violated
as I do right now.

00:18:14.059 --> 00:18:16.493
Whether you believe me
or not is beside the point.

00:18:16.562 --> 00:18:17.790
A year and a half ago,

00:18:17.863 --> 00:18:20.491
the only solution was
to rewrite your program.

00:18:20.566 --> 00:18:23.296
I have to perform
that same procedure now.

00:18:23.368 --> 00:18:24.733
That isn't fair.

00:18:24.803 --> 00:18:26.737
You're malfunctioning

00:18:26.805 --> 00:18:28.898
and you need to be repaired.

00:18:29.007 --> 00:18:32.170
Return to Sick Bay
and wait for my orders.

00:18:57.436 --> 00:18:58.368
Doctor.

00:18:58.437 --> 00:19:00.166
What's happening?

00:19:00.239 --> 00:19:02.104
What are you doing?

00:19:02.174 --> 00:19:03.869
Lieutenant Torres
requires a copy

00:19:03.942 --> 00:19:05.569
of your most recent
memory files,

00:19:05.644 --> 00:19:06.804
including the backups.

00:19:06.879 --> 00:19:08.471
You're going
to rewrite my program.

00:19:08.547 --> 00:19:10.310
The Captain thinks
it's for the best.

00:19:10.382 --> 00:19:11.781
I'm sorry.

00:19:11.850 --> 00:19:12.782
B'Elanna and Seven

00:19:12.851 --> 00:19:14.512
are setting up the procedure
right now.

00:19:14.586 --> 00:19:16.486
In the meantime, you're to brief

00:19:16.555 --> 00:19:19.854
Mr. Paris about any experiments
you're performing, any tests.

00:19:19.925 --> 00:19:21.722
I'll be filling in
while your program's off-line.

00:19:27.065 --> 00:19:31.468
Okay. So, you're running
some kind of cell analysis?

00:19:31.537 --> 00:19:33.004
Yes.

00:19:33.071 --> 00:19:34.402
Well, let's take a look.

00:19:34.473 --> 00:19:36.031
What happened 18 months ago?

00:19:36.108 --> 00:19:37.075
Doc...

00:19:37.142 --> 00:19:38.837
Why won't the Captain tell me?

00:19:39.912 --> 00:19:41.675
She has her reasons.

00:19:41.747 --> 00:19:43.510
And you agree with her?

00:19:45.150 --> 00:19:49.553
I was there... and, yes,
I agree with her.

00:20:24.623 --> 00:20:25.954
Come in.

00:20:29.795 --> 00:20:32.889
Are you having
a little trouble regenerating?

00:20:32.965 --> 00:20:36.332
My alcove is
functioning properly.

00:20:36.401 --> 00:20:39.564
I am having trouble with
the nature of individuality.

00:20:41.206 --> 00:20:44.073
There's a time and a place
for philosophical discussion.

00:20:44.142 --> 00:20:46.576
2:00 in the morning in my
quarters isn't one of them,

00:20:46.645 --> 00:20:48.078
but I'll tell you what.

00:20:48.146 --> 00:20:49.977
Meet me in the Mess Hall
tomorrow...

00:20:50.082 --> 00:20:51.572
Tomorrow will be too late.

00:20:51.650 --> 00:20:54.915
We'll have already rewritten
the Doctor's program by then.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:01.088
And violated his rights
as an individual.

00:21:01.159 --> 00:21:03.059
Precisely.

00:21:03.128 --> 00:21:05.688
If you've come to act
as my conscience,

00:21:05.764 --> 00:21:07.231
you're a little late.

00:21:07.299 --> 00:21:09.927
I considered these issues
18 months ago,

00:21:10.035 --> 00:21:12.162
as I did again this morning.

00:21:12.237 --> 00:21:14.535
I came to the same conclusion.

00:21:14.606 --> 00:21:16.233
Your conclusion is wrong.

00:21:21.913 --> 00:21:24.279
Coffee, black.

00:21:32.758 --> 00:21:33.952
Lukewarm.

00:21:34.026 --> 00:21:36.358
Now I've told that replicator
a dozen times

00:21:36.428 --> 00:21:38.623
about the temperature
of my coffee.

00:21:38.697 --> 00:21:41.598
It just doesn't seem
to want to listen...

00:21:41.667 --> 00:21:44.158
almost as if it's got
a mind of its own,

00:21:44.236 --> 00:21:46.170
but it doesn't.

00:21:46.238 --> 00:21:47.762
A replicator operates

00:21:47.839 --> 00:21:50.706
through a series
of electronic pathways

00:21:50.776 --> 00:21:52.209
that allow it

00:21:52.277 --> 00:21:55.371
to receive instructions
and take appropriate action,

00:21:55.447 --> 00:21:57.677
and there you go...
a cup of coffee,

00:21:57.749 --> 00:21:59.979
a bowl of soup,
a plasma conduit...

00:22:00.085 --> 00:22:02.053
whatever we tell it to do.

00:22:02.120 --> 00:22:06.250
As difficult as it is
to accept...

00:22:06.325 --> 00:22:08.816
the Doctor is
more like that replicator

00:22:08.894 --> 00:22:09.928
than he is like us.

00:22:09.928 --> 00:22:10.394
Than he is like us.

00:22:10.462 --> 00:22:11.895
He would disagree.

00:22:11.963 --> 00:22:13.157
I'm sure he would,

00:22:13.231 --> 00:22:16.098
but I can't let that change
my decision.

00:22:16.168 --> 00:22:17.795
I learned that the hard way

00:22:17.869 --> 00:22:20.201
when his program
almost self-destructed.

00:22:20.272 --> 00:22:22.035
I won't take that risk again.

00:22:22.107 --> 00:22:24.075
The risk isn't yours to take.

00:22:24.142 --> 00:22:27.134
If one of my crew
chose to put a phaser

00:22:27.212 --> 00:22:29.840
to his own head,
should I let him?

00:22:29.915 --> 00:22:32.406
It would depend
on the situation.

00:22:32.484 --> 00:22:35.885
It always depends
on the situation, Seven,

00:22:35.954 --> 00:22:39.412
but we can debate
philosophy another time.

00:22:41.493 --> 00:22:43.927
When you separated me
from the collective,

00:22:43.995 --> 00:22:45.257
I was an unknown risk

00:22:45.330 --> 00:22:48.857
to your crew,
yet you kept me on board,

00:22:48.934 --> 00:22:51.402
you allowed me to evolve
into an individual.

00:22:51.470 --> 00:22:53.301
You're a human being.

00:22:53.372 --> 00:22:55.101
He's a hologram.

00:22:55.173 --> 00:22:58.404
And you allowed that hologram
to evolve as well,

00:22:58.477 --> 00:23:00.741
to exceed
his original programming,

00:23:00.812 --> 00:23:02.905
and yet, now you choose
to abandon him.

00:23:02.981 --> 00:23:05.677
Objection noted.

00:23:05.751 --> 00:23:07.582
Good night.

00:23:12.324 --> 00:23:14.019
It is unsettling.

00:23:16.495 --> 00:23:20.727
You say that I am a human being
and yet, I am also Borg...

00:23:20.799 --> 00:23:23.791
part of me not unlike
your replicator...

00:23:23.869 --> 00:23:27.566
not unlike the Doctor.

00:23:27.639 --> 00:23:31.405
Will you one day choose
to abandon me as well?

00:23:31.476 --> 00:23:33.603
I have always looked

00:23:33.678 --> 00:23:39.139
to you as my example...
my guide to humanity.

00:23:39.217 --> 00:23:42.516
Perhaps I've been mistaken.

00:23:42.587 --> 00:23:44.487
Good night.

00:24:11.616 --> 00:24:14.710
I'd like to think I made
my decision 18 months ago

00:24:14.786 --> 00:24:16.413
for all the right reasons.

00:24:16.488 --> 00:24:21.858
The truth is, my own biases
about what you are

00:24:21.927 --> 00:24:24.623
have just as much
to do with it.

00:24:24.696 --> 00:24:25.890
At the very least,

00:24:25.964 --> 00:24:28.933
you deserve to know
exactly what happened...

00:24:29.034 --> 00:24:31.195
if you're willing.

00:24:44.783 --> 00:24:46.250
I'm ready.

00:25:03.635 --> 00:25:05.569
You're standing on my foot.

00:25:05.637 --> 00:25:06.831
I am not.

00:25:06.905 --> 00:25:08.304
Shh...

00:25:09.941 --> 00:25:11.135
If you ask me,
they should have

00:25:11.209 --> 00:25:12.301
just locked the turbolift...

00:25:12.377 --> 00:25:14.140
Neelix...
the power's down.

00:25:14.212 --> 00:25:16.578
Jetal to Torres.

00:25:16.648 --> 00:25:18.172
Uh, go ahead, Ensign.

00:25:18.250 --> 00:25:20.445
Or should I say...

00:25:20.519 --> 00:25:22.453
Surprise!

00:25:32.764 --> 00:25:34.493
I'm going to kill you.

00:25:36.201 --> 00:25:37.429
I want you to go along

00:25:37.502 --> 00:25:39.333
on a few
of the shuttle surveys...

00:25:39.404 --> 00:25:40.769
if I can talk you into it.

00:25:40.839 --> 00:25:41.931
Another away mission?

00:25:42.040 --> 00:25:43.234
Certainly.
I'm flattered.

00:25:43.308 --> 00:25:44.673
I guess
the birthday girl and I

00:25:44.743 --> 00:25:46.506
get the pleasure
of your company, Doc.

00:25:46.578 --> 00:25:48.409
You launch at 1900 hours,

00:25:48.480 --> 00:25:49.538
Shuttle Bay 1.

00:25:51.149 --> 00:25:52.446
Hello, Doctor.

00:25:52.517 --> 00:25:53.916
Ensign Jetal.

00:25:53.985 --> 00:25:56.078
I haven't seen you in months.

00:25:56.154 --> 00:25:58.486
The price I pay
for staying in good health.

00:25:58.557 --> 00:26:01.754
So, keeping busy
down on Deck 11?

00:26:01.826 --> 00:26:03.054
Too busy.

00:26:03.128 --> 00:26:05.358
We're modifying
one of the shuttles,

00:26:05.430 --> 00:26:08.092
making it more maneuverable
and more... cool.

00:26:08.166 --> 00:26:11.465
Hmm... I see you've been working
with Mr. Paris.

00:26:11.536 --> 00:26:13.163
My condolences.

00:26:13.238 --> 00:26:16.833
I thought I picked up
a slight distortion in subspace,

00:26:16.908 --> 00:26:18.899
but it's not there anymore.

00:26:18.977 --> 00:26:20.877
Nothing on
our long-range sensors,

00:26:20.946 --> 00:26:22.345
but a few hydrogen atoms.

00:26:24.516 --> 00:26:26.143
Candid shot?

00:26:26.217 --> 00:26:27.684
Try to look natural.

00:26:27.752 --> 00:26:29.549
At least it's my good side.

00:26:33.658 --> 00:26:35.421
Let's get one of the group.

00:26:43.702 --> 00:26:45.636
This is the last one.

00:26:45.704 --> 00:26:46.728
Say "Cheese."

00:26:46.805 --> 00:26:47.931
Cheese.

00:26:48.006 --> 00:26:50.031
Doctor, I have a shuttle to fly.

00:26:50.108 --> 00:26:51.370
Ah, yes.

00:26:54.045 --> 00:26:55.706
What was that?

00:26:55.780 --> 00:26:57.338
Our sensors are dead.

00:26:57.415 --> 00:26:58.347
Power's being drained.

00:26:58.416 --> 00:26:59.883
Shields and weapons
are off-line.

00:26:59.951 --> 00:27:00.815
How?!

00:27:34.185 --> 00:27:35.743
Doctor to Voyager.
Mayday.

00:27:35.820 --> 00:27:37.515
We're under attack!

00:27:37.589 --> 00:27:38.851
I've got wounded.
Mayday!

00:27:38.923 --> 00:27:40.413
Acknowledged, Doctor.

00:27:40.492 --> 00:27:42.585
Set navigational controls
to return to Voyager.

00:27:42.661 --> 00:27:43.821
Commander, can you hear me?

00:27:43.895 --> 00:27:44.919
Doctor, please respond.

00:27:45.063 --> 00:27:46.155
Hello?!

00:27:46.231 --> 00:27:47.926
Computer,
engage auto navigation.

00:27:48.066 --> 00:27:50.364
Lay in a course for Voyager,
full impulse.

00:27:50.435 --> 00:27:51.367
Doctor...

00:27:51.436 --> 00:27:52.368
Stay calm.

00:27:52.437 --> 00:27:54.928
That weapon carried
quite a punch.

00:27:55.073 --> 00:27:56.301
Is she okay?

00:27:56.374 --> 00:27:58.274
She's unconscious.

00:27:58.343 --> 00:27:59.742
Voyager...

00:27:59.811 --> 00:28:01.438
We've lost contact.

00:28:03.481 --> 00:28:05.073
I sent that alien
back to his ship.

00:28:05.150 --> 00:28:06.515
You think they'd be grateful.

00:28:06.584 --> 00:28:09.747
You should have beamed...
him... into space.

00:28:09.821 --> 00:28:12.915
I'm not in the business
of killing people, Ensign.

00:28:14.492 --> 00:28:15.686
Synaptic shock?

00:28:15.760 --> 00:28:17.921
But there was no neural damage.

00:28:19.397 --> 00:28:20.864
Mr. Kim!

00:28:20.932 --> 00:28:22.456
I don't understand!

00:28:25.704 --> 00:28:27.365
Oh, no!

00:28:33.445 --> 00:28:36.539
Doctor, stand by for transport.

00:28:36.614 --> 00:28:38.878
Beam us directly to Sick Bay.

00:28:44.689 --> 00:28:47.089
Prepare these people
for surgery.

00:28:51.229 --> 00:28:52.662
Here, what happened?

00:28:52.731 --> 00:28:53.789
We were fired on.

00:28:53.865 --> 00:28:55.696
There's something wrong
with their nervous systems.

00:28:55.767 --> 00:28:57.428
We've got to stabilize
their synapses.

00:28:57.502 --> 00:28:59.129
Get me a choline compound.

00:28:59.204 --> 00:29:00.193
Which choline compound?

00:29:00.271 --> 00:29:01.329
It doesn't matter.

00:29:01.406 --> 00:29:02.930
Just make sure it's a pure base.

00:29:08.413 --> 00:29:11.177
Her spinal cord's deteriorating.

00:29:13.618 --> 00:29:15.984
Same rate of collapse.

00:29:16.054 --> 00:29:19.581
Acetylcholine...
25 microliters.

00:29:22.727 --> 00:29:23.887
It's not helping.

00:29:23.962 --> 00:29:25.691
I'm reading
massive synaptic failure.

00:29:26.765 --> 00:29:28.790
This doesn't make any sense.

00:29:29.868 --> 00:29:31.392
Paris to Engineering.

00:29:31.469 --> 00:29:33.869
Transfer all available power
to Sick Bay.

00:29:33.938 --> 00:29:35.235
Acknowledged.

00:29:36.374 --> 00:29:37.898
Some kind of plasmic energy

00:29:37.976 --> 00:29:40.376
is arcing between
their neural membranes.

00:29:40.445 --> 00:29:43.778
That weapon...
it was designed to do this.

00:29:43.848 --> 00:29:46.681
To leave a residual charge
in the victim's body?

00:29:46.751 --> 00:29:49.185
An energy pulse that remains
in the neural membranes,

00:29:49.254 --> 00:29:50.881
working its way
up the spinal cord

00:29:50.955 --> 00:29:52.422
and into the brain.

00:29:52.490 --> 00:29:53.787
They'll be dead in minutes

00:29:53.858 --> 00:29:55.553
if we don't find a way
to stop it.

00:29:55.627 --> 00:29:57.686
I've got to protect
their brain functions.

00:29:57.762 --> 00:29:59.195
His neocortex is failing.

00:29:59.264 --> 00:30:00.629
A spinal shunt.

00:30:00.698 --> 00:30:03.826
I'll isolate the spinal cord
from the brain stem...

00:30:03.902 --> 00:30:05.529
until I can repair
the cellular damage.

00:30:05.603 --> 00:30:08.299
But I don't have time to perform
the procedure on both of them.

00:30:08.373 --> 00:30:09.305
Then talk me through it.

00:30:09.374 --> 00:30:10.306
We'll do them together.

00:30:10.375 --> 00:30:11.307
It's too complex.

00:30:11.376 --> 00:30:12.365
Then make a choice,

00:30:12.443 --> 00:30:13.671
before we lose them both!

00:30:20.018 --> 00:30:22.418
Subdermal scalpel.

00:30:30.428 --> 00:30:32.419
Bioelectric field generator.

00:30:40.071 --> 00:30:41.732
His vital signs
are stabilizing...

00:30:45.210 --> 00:30:46.575
It's working.

00:30:46.644 --> 00:30:47.906
Cellular regenerator.

00:30:58.022 --> 00:31:01.082
His neural membranes
are reestablishing themselves.

00:31:01.159 --> 00:31:03.354
Good... good.

00:31:25.984 --> 00:31:27.884
The attack...

00:31:27.952 --> 00:31:30.580
how did it end?

00:31:30.655 --> 00:31:32.418
Were there more casualties?

00:31:34.025 --> 00:31:37.893
We exchanged fire
for another few minutes,

00:31:37.962 --> 00:31:40.362
then the aliens withdrew.

00:31:40.431 --> 00:31:43.662
There was only one casualty...

00:31:43.735 --> 00:31:45.259
Ensign Jetal.

00:31:48.606 --> 00:31:50.437
I don't mean to seem unfeeling,

00:31:50.508 --> 00:31:53.602
but I'm programmed to accept
the loss of a patient

00:31:53.678 --> 00:31:55.805
with professional detachment.

00:32:08.693 --> 00:32:10.354
We are assembled here today

00:32:10.428 --> 00:32:13.158
to pay final respects
to our honored dead...

00:32:13.231 --> 00:32:15.597
Ensign Ahni Jetal.

00:32:15.667 --> 00:32:20.434
Her intelligence and her charm
have made our long journey home

00:32:20.505 --> 00:32:22.166
seem not quite so long.

00:32:22.240 --> 00:32:25.505
As she continues
on a journey of her own,

00:32:25.576 --> 00:32:28.136
we will keep her
in our hearts...

00:32:28.212 --> 00:32:30.009
and in our memories.

00:32:39.557 --> 00:32:41.388
We're low
on synthetic antigens

00:32:41.459 --> 00:32:42.926
and I'm sorry to report,

00:32:42.994 --> 00:32:45.189
many of the medicinal plants
you've collected

00:32:45.263 --> 00:32:47.527
over the past several months
were destroyed as well.

00:32:47.598 --> 00:32:50.158
I have some herbs in storage
you might be able to use.

00:32:50.234 --> 00:32:51.826
Been holding out on me?

00:32:51.903 --> 00:32:52.961
No.

00:32:53.037 --> 00:32:54.937
I was keeping them
around just in case.

00:32:55.006 --> 00:32:56.337
Good planning.

00:32:56.407 --> 00:32:58.272
As for the antigens,
I'll have

00:32:58.343 --> 00:33:00.709
to start replicating
them in batches.

00:33:00.778 --> 00:33:02.871
Which do you want first?

00:33:02.947 --> 00:33:05.415
Decisions, decisions.

00:33:10.054 --> 00:33:11.681
How do you make
a decision, Mr. Neelix?

00:33:11.756 --> 00:33:13.883
In general, I mean.

00:33:13.958 --> 00:33:17.917
I guess I weigh the alternatives
and try to decide which is best.

00:33:18.062 --> 00:33:21.828
Which is best?

00:33:21.899 --> 00:33:23.924
How do you determine that?

00:33:24.068 --> 00:33:26.195
I never thought about it,
really.

00:33:26.270 --> 00:33:27.897
Well, maybe you should...

00:33:27.972 --> 00:33:29.906
think about it, I mean.

00:33:29.974 --> 00:33:32.272
I guess every situation
is a little different.

00:33:32.343 --> 00:33:33.935
For me, it's rather simple.

00:33:34.012 --> 00:33:35.877
While I'm faced
with a decision,

00:33:35.947 --> 00:33:37.915
my program calculates
the variables

00:33:37.982 --> 00:33:39.074
and I take action.

00:33:39.150 --> 00:33:41.710
For example, what
could be simpler

00:33:41.786 --> 00:33:43.845
then a triage situation
in Sick Bay?

00:33:43.921 --> 00:33:48.119
Two patients, for example,
both injured, for example,

00:33:48.192 --> 00:33:51.423
both in imminent
danger of dying.

00:33:51.496 --> 00:33:53.464
Calculate the variables.

00:33:53.531 --> 00:33:57.092
My program needs to
ascertain which patient

00:33:57.168 --> 00:34:00.069
has the greater
chance of survival,

00:34:00.138 --> 00:34:01.833
and that's the one I treat.

00:34:02.874 --> 00:34:04.034
- Oh!
- Oh!

00:34:04.108 --> 00:34:05.905
Simple.

00:34:05.977 --> 00:34:12.041
But... what if they have
an equal chance of survival?

00:34:12.116 --> 00:34:14.516
What then?

00:34:14.585 --> 00:34:15.882
Hmm?

00:34:15.953 --> 00:34:17.352
Flip a coin?

00:34:17.422 --> 00:34:18.753
Pick a card?

00:34:18.823 --> 00:34:19.657
Doctor...

00:34:19.891 --> 00:34:20.880
Oh, I'm all right.

00:34:20.958 --> 00:34:22.448
I'm a hologram.
I don't get injured.

00:34:22.527 --> 00:34:24.757
I don't feel pain.
I don't die.

00:34:24.829 --> 00:34:27.889
Unlike some people
I could tell you about.

00:34:27.965 --> 00:34:30.661
For example, two patients,

00:34:30.735 --> 00:34:31.929
both injured,

00:34:32.003 --> 00:34:36.531
both in imminent danger of...

00:34:36.607 --> 00:34:38.336
Don't touch me.

00:34:38.409 --> 00:34:39.569
I'm a hologram.

00:34:39.644 --> 00:34:41.441
Photonic energy.
Don't waste your time.

00:34:41.512 --> 00:34:42.740
Neelix to Security.

00:34:42.814 --> 00:34:44.076
Send a team
to the Mess Hall, please.

00:34:44.148 --> 00:34:46.912
A whole team, Mr. Neelix?

00:34:46.984 --> 00:34:49.475
Throwing a little party,
are we?

00:34:49.554 --> 00:34:52.785
Why, I attended a party
just recently.

00:34:52.857 --> 00:34:55.883
A birthday party
for a very nice young woman.

00:34:55.960 --> 00:34:59.293
I made a decision there, too.

00:34:59.363 --> 00:35:00.830
Several of them, in fact.

00:35:00.898 --> 00:35:02.593
When I came through the door,

00:35:02.667 --> 00:35:03.759
do I turn right

00:35:03.835 --> 00:35:05.268
or do I turn left?

00:35:05.336 --> 00:35:08.794
As I recall, I decided on...
the latter.

00:35:08.873 --> 00:35:10.135
Then, what should
I see before me,

00:35:10.208 --> 00:35:11.266
but the hors d'oeuvre tray?

00:35:11.342 --> 00:35:12.604
And another decision...

00:35:12.677 --> 00:35:17.080
"Do I take a canapé...
or refuse?"

00:35:17.148 --> 00:35:19.116
Oh. That's an easy one.
I'm a hologram... I don't eat.

00:35:19.183 --> 00:35:20.673
Something's wrong with him.

00:35:20.751 --> 00:35:21.683
Don't you know it's rude

00:35:21.752 --> 00:35:23.242
to refer to somebody
in the third person?

00:35:23.321 --> 00:35:25.152
You had a choice, Mr. Neelix...

00:35:25.223 --> 00:35:27.817
"Should I do something rude
or not do something rude?"

00:35:27.892 --> 00:35:30.793
Doctor, we must return
to Sick Bay.

00:35:30.862 --> 00:35:32.090
Why should I?

00:35:32.163 --> 00:35:34.290
What if I don't want
to return to Sick Bay?

00:35:34.365 --> 00:35:38.233
What if I decide
not to return to Sick Bay?

00:35:38.302 --> 00:35:40.532
No. I don't choose this.

00:35:40.605 --> 00:35:42.402
Leave me alone! Let me go!

00:35:42.473 --> 00:35:44.031
Why did she have to die?

00:35:44.108 --> 00:35:45.302
Why did I kill her?!

00:35:45.376 --> 00:35:47.241
Why did I decide to kill her?!
Why?!

00:35:47.311 --> 00:35:48.835
Somebody tell me why!

00:35:48.913 --> 00:35:51.575
It was downhill from there.

00:35:51.649 --> 00:35:53.583
You developed a feedback loop

00:35:53.651 --> 00:35:56.176
between your ethical
and cognitive subroutines.

00:35:56.254 --> 00:35:58.051
You were having
the same thoughts

00:35:58.122 --> 00:35:59.214
over and over again.

00:35:59.290 --> 00:36:00.780
We couldn't stop it.

00:36:00.858 --> 00:36:04.259
Our only option was to erase
your memories of those events.

00:36:04.328 --> 00:36:06.262
You were right.

00:36:06.330 --> 00:36:09.026
I didn't deserve
to keep those memories...

00:36:09.100 --> 00:36:10.431
not after what I did.

00:36:10.501 --> 00:36:12.366
You were performing your duty.

00:36:12.436 --> 00:36:14.563
Two patients... which do I kill?

00:36:14.639 --> 00:36:16.630
- Doctor...
- "Doctor"? Hardly.

00:36:16.707 --> 00:36:19.232
A doctor retains
his objectivity.

00:36:19.310 --> 00:36:20.902
I didn't do that, did I?

00:36:21.012 --> 00:36:23.640
Two patients,
equal chances of survival,

00:36:23.714 --> 00:36:25.909
and I chose the one
I was closer to?

00:36:26.050 --> 00:36:27.312
I chose my friend?

00:36:27.385 --> 00:36:28.852
That's not in my programming.

00:36:28.920 --> 00:36:30.888
That's not what I was designed
to do!

00:36:30.955 --> 00:36:32.047
Go ahead!

00:36:32.123 --> 00:36:33.750
Reprogram me!
I'll lend you a hand!

00:36:33.824 --> 00:36:35.257
Let's start with this very day,

00:36:35.326 --> 00:36:36.418
this hour, this second!

00:36:36.494 --> 00:36:39.122
Computer, deactivate the EMH.

00:36:43.301 --> 00:36:45.132
Here we go again.

00:36:47.705 --> 00:36:49.468
Captain?

00:36:49.540 --> 00:36:53.476
It's as though there's a battle
being fought inside him...

00:36:53.544 --> 00:36:56.638
between his original programming

00:36:56.714 --> 00:36:59.740
and what he's become.

00:36:59.817 --> 00:37:04.379
Our solution was
to end that battle.

00:37:04.455 --> 00:37:06.582
What if we were wrong?

00:37:06.657 --> 00:37:08.591
We've seen what happens to him.

00:37:08.659 --> 00:37:10.490
In fact, we've seen it twice.

00:37:10.561 --> 00:37:14.861
Still... we allowed him
to evolve,

00:37:14.932 --> 00:37:17.366
and at the first sign
of trouble...

00:37:22.340 --> 00:37:26.106
We gave him a soul, B'Elanna.

00:37:26.177 --> 00:37:28.907
Do we have the right
to take it away now?

00:37:29.046 --> 00:37:32.846
We gave him
personality subroutines.

00:37:32.917 --> 00:37:35.112
I'd hardly call that a soul.

00:38:14.792 --> 00:38:16.054
Captain.

00:38:16.127 --> 00:38:18.857
I'm having trouble...

00:38:18.929 --> 00:38:21.727
with the nature
of individuality.

00:38:21.799 --> 00:38:24.632
You require
a philosophical discussion.

00:38:24.702 --> 00:38:26.533
There's a time
and a place for it.

00:38:26.604 --> 00:38:28.231
This is one of them.

00:38:31.275 --> 00:38:34.176
After I freed you
from the collective...

00:38:35.880 --> 00:38:39.179
you were transformed.

00:38:39.250 --> 00:38:41.684
It's been a difficult process.

00:38:43.220 --> 00:38:45.085
Was it worth it?

00:38:45.156 --> 00:38:47.056
I had no choice.

00:38:47.124 --> 00:38:48.819
That's not what I asked you.

00:38:52.229 --> 00:38:54.561
If I could
change what happened...

00:38:54.632 --> 00:38:57.760
erase what you did to me...
would I?

00:39:02.173 --> 00:39:03.538
No.

00:39:06.243 --> 00:39:09.235
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:39:09.313 --> 00:39:12.077
Our Doctor is now our patient.

00:39:12.149 --> 00:39:14.083
It's been two weeks
since I've ordered

00:39:14.151 --> 00:39:15.880
a 'round-the-clock vigil.

00:39:15.986 --> 00:39:18.853
A crew member has stayed
with him at all times,

00:39:18.923 --> 00:39:22.381
offering a sounding board
and a familiar presence,

00:39:22.460 --> 00:39:24.121
while he struggles
to understand

00:39:24.195 --> 00:39:26.425
his memories and his thoughts.

00:39:26.497 --> 00:39:30.263
The chances of recovery...
uncertain.

00:39:41.011 --> 00:39:44.208
The more I think about it,
the more I realize

00:39:44.281 --> 00:39:47.444
there's nothing I could've
done differently.

00:39:50.020 --> 00:39:51.817
What do you mean?

00:39:51.889 --> 00:39:56.622
The primordial atom burst,
sending out its radiation,

00:39:56.694 --> 00:39:58.924
setting everything in motion.

00:39:59.029 --> 00:40:01.623
One particle
collides with another,

00:40:01.699 --> 00:40:04.497
gases expand, planets contract

00:40:04.568 --> 00:40:06.126
and before you know it,

00:40:06.203 --> 00:40:08.501
we've got starships
and holodecks

00:40:08.572 --> 00:40:10.699
and... chicken soup.

00:40:10.775 --> 00:40:14.643
In fact, you can't help
but have starships

00:40:14.712 --> 00:40:16.475
and holodecks
and chicken soup,

00:40:16.547 --> 00:40:20.039
because it was all determined
20 billion years ago!

00:40:20.117 --> 00:40:23.143
There is a certain
logic to your logic.

00:40:25.523 --> 00:40:26.922
Progress?

00:40:26.991 --> 00:40:29.926
I'm not sure if he's making
any sense of this experience,

00:40:29.994 --> 00:40:32.792
or if his program's
just running in circles.

00:40:32.863 --> 00:40:34.854
You've been here for 16 hours.

00:40:34.932 --> 00:40:37.628
Let me continue while you rest.

00:40:37.701 --> 00:40:39.635
I'll be all right.

00:40:39.703 --> 00:40:41.671
Go back to the Bridge.

00:40:54.518 --> 00:40:56.986
How can you read
at a time like this?

00:40:57.087 --> 00:40:59.214
It helps me think.

00:40:59.323 --> 00:41:02.315
Think? What do you need
to think about?

00:41:02.393 --> 00:41:07.023
You. This book is relevant
to your situation.

00:41:07.097 --> 00:41:10.066
Oh? What is it?

00:41:11.869 --> 00:41:14.633
Poetry... written on Earth

00:41:14.705 --> 00:41:19.404
a thousand years ago...
La Vita Nuova.

00:41:19.477 --> 00:41:22.878
La Vita Nuova...
"The New Life"? Ha!

00:41:22.947 --> 00:41:25.211
Tell that to Ensign Jetal.

00:41:26.417 --> 00:41:28.510
Actually...

00:41:28.586 --> 00:41:29.253
I killed her countless times.

00:41:29.253 --> 00:41:30.686
I killed her countless times.

00:41:32.723 --> 00:41:34.588
What do you mean?

00:41:34.658 --> 00:41:37.889
Causality, probability.

00:41:37.962 --> 00:41:42.058
For every action, there's
an infinite number of reactions,

00:41:42.132 --> 00:41:45.898
and in each one of them,
I killed her!

00:41:48.772 --> 00:41:50.740
Or did I?

00:41:55.246 --> 00:41:58.010
Too many possibilities...

00:41:59.416 --> 00:42:02.408
too many pathways
for my program to follow...

00:42:04.355 --> 00:42:06.516
impossible to choose...

00:42:10.060 --> 00:42:12.722
Still, I...

00:42:12.796 --> 00:42:16.232
I can't live with the knowledge
of what I've done.

00:42:16.300 --> 00:42:18.268
I can't.

00:42:20.704 --> 00:42:22.171
Captain?

00:42:26.410 --> 00:42:28.503
- Captain?
- Oh, sorry.

00:42:28.579 --> 00:42:30.774
How could you sleep
at a time like this?

00:42:30.848 --> 00:42:32.372
Well, it's been a long day.

00:42:32.449 --> 00:42:33.677
You were saying?

00:42:33.751 --> 00:42:34.775
What's wrong?

00:42:34.852 --> 00:42:36.217
Nothing.

00:42:36.287 --> 00:42:37.379
You're ill.

00:42:37.454 --> 00:42:38.546
I have a headache.

00:42:38.622 --> 00:42:39.714
Fever. You have

00:42:39.790 --> 00:42:41.382
- a fever.
- I'll live.

00:42:41.458 --> 00:42:42.755
- Medical emergency!
- Doctor...

00:42:42.826 --> 00:42:44.657
Someone's got to treat you
immediately.

00:42:44.728 --> 00:42:47.390
Call Mr. Paris.
You've got to get to Sick Bay!

00:42:47.464 --> 00:42:48.431
Doctor...

00:42:49.733 --> 00:42:52.361
I'm a little busy right now...

00:42:52.436 --> 00:42:54.461
helping a friend.

00:42:59.510 --> 00:43:03.105
I... I'll be all right.

00:43:03.180 --> 00:43:07.446
Go. Sleep. Please.

00:43:07.518 --> 00:43:09.577
I'll still be here
in the morning.

00:43:09.653 --> 00:43:11.917
Sure?

00:43:12.056 --> 00:43:14.684
Yes. Please.

00:43:14.758 --> 00:43:18.694
I don't want to be responsible
for any more suffering.

00:43:35.846 --> 00:43:38.110
Good night.

00:43:38.182 --> 00:43:39.945
If you need anything...

00:43:40.050 --> 00:43:41.517
I'll call.

00:43:41.585 --> 00:43:43.052
Thank you, Captain.

00:44:25.863 --> 00:44:32.132
"In that book
which is my memory...

00:44:32.202 --> 00:44:34.796
"On the first page
of the chapter

00:44:34.872 --> 00:44:38.808
"that is the day
when I first met you...

00:44:40.844 --> 00:44:47.079
Appear the words,
'Here begins a new life."'
